---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import axon from "~/assets/img/massing-axon-crop.jpg";
import { site, program, offering } from "~/data/project";
---

<section class="section opportunity" aria-labelledby="opp-h">
  <div class="shell grid">
    <div class="text" data-reveal>
      <p class="eyebrow">The opportunity</p>
      <h2 id="opp-h" class="display-l">
        Thirty-eight homes, engineered and in review, five minutes from the shipyard.
      </h2>

      <div class="prose measure">
        <p>
          Four parcels on Carr Boulevard at Kitsap Way have been assembled into a single
          {" "}{site.totalAcres}-acre development site — {site.totalSF.toLocaleString()} square feet,
          zoned {site.zoning.toLowerCase()}. The plat lays out {program.totalUnits} lots for
          fee-simple attached single-family homes across six plan types, with
          {" "}{site.openSpaceSF.toLocaleString()} SF of open space in tracts {site.tracts},
          {" "}{site.guestStalls} guest stalls and a stormwater pond.
        </p>
        <p>
          The work a builder would otherwise carry has been done. Signed preliminary civil
          improvement plans, a geotechnical report, a storm drainage analysis, a traffic count,
          a tree report, a photometric plan, a utility availability letter and full architecture
          for all thirty-eight homes went to the City of Bremerton on August 5, 2026 with the
          preliminary plat and site development permit application. That package is in review now.
        </p>
        <p>
          The offer is structured so that review risk stays with the seller.
          {" "}{offering.closingCondition} — {offering.closingNote.toLowerCase()}
          {" "}Unit lot subdivision is an active part of the entitlement approach, which is what
          lets a builder convey each attached home fee-simple rather than as a condominium.
        </p>
        <p>
          The six-lot parcel on the commercial frontage carries its own optionality: hold it,
          build it for sale, or dispose of it separately, without touching the thirty-two lots behind.
        </p>
      </div>

      <a class="inline-link" href="/offering">Read the full offering summary</a>
    </div>

    <figure class="fig" data-reveal data-reveal-image>
      <Image
        src={axon}
        alt="Axonometric massing study of the thirty-eight attached homes on the Carr Boulevard plat, with Kitsap Way along the north edge and the private drive loop through the centre."
        widths={[600, 900, 1300]}
        sizes="(max-width: 960px) 92vw, 42vw"
        quality={78}
        format="avif"
      />
      <figcaption>
        Massing study over the preliminary plat layout. Thirty-two lots on parcels 2–4, six on the
        General Commercial frontage parcel.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 0.92fr);
    gap: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 6rem);
    align-items: start;
  }
  @media (max-width: 960px) { .grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }

  h2 { margin-bottom: 2.25rem; max-width: 18ch; }
  .prose { color: var(--muted); }
  .prose p:first-child { color: var(--ink); font-size: 1.125rem; }

  .inline-link {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-top: 2rem;
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    text-decoration: none;
    color: var(--brass-ink);
    border-bottom: 1px solid currentColor;
    padding-bottom: 0.2rem;
  }

  .fig { margin: 0; position: sticky; top: 6rem; }
  @media (max-width: 960px) { .fig { position: static; } }
  .fig :global(img) {
    width: 100%;
    background: var(--paper-2);
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  figcaption {
    margin-top: 0.9rem;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--muted);
    max-width: 44ch;
  }
</style>
